  "correct": "3",
  "solution": "The logic followed here is : **(2nd number + 3rd number) = 1st number**\n\n**Given :**\n\n \n• (23, 14, 9)\n\n14 + 9 = 23\n\n23 = 23 (LHS = RHS)\n\nAnd,\n\n \n• (37, 19, 18)\n\n​19 + 18 = 37\n\n37 = 37 (LHS = RHS)\n\nSo,\n\n \n• Option - (1) : (125, 25, 5)\n\n25 + 5 = 125\n\n**30 ≠ 125 (LHS ≠ RHS)**\n\n \n• Option - (2) : (125, 100, 5)\n\n100 + 5 = 125\n\n**105** ≠ 125 (LHS ≠ RHS)\n\n \n• Option - (3) : (125, 25, 100)\n\n25 + 100 = 125\n\n**125 = 125 (LHS = RHS)**\n\n \n• Option - (4) : (125, 5, 25)\n\n5 + 25 = 125\n\n30 ≠ 125 (LHS ≠ RHS)\n\nHence, **\"Option - (3)\"** is the correct answer.",
